title: A Courier from the North
subtitle: Money arrives from Moscow, in a suitcase.
new-page: true
tags: event
priority: -1
view-if: {!
if (typeof RG === 'undefined') { return false; }
if (!RG.lw && this.game.scenes.lw_lib) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
return !!(RG.lw && RG.lw.ready('m_suitcase'));
!}
on-arrival: {!
if (!RG.lw) { this._runActions(this.game.scenes.lw_lib.onArrival); }
RG.lw.fire('m_suitcase');
Q.lw_amount = RG.lw.rnd(2, 3);
Q.lw_name = RG.pick(['diamonds sewn into the lining', 'dollar notes under a false bottom', 'Tsarist gold roubles in a box of cigars', 'pearls in a tin of Russian tea']);
!}

= A Courier from the North

A Finnish sailor with a cardboard suitcase came off the Stettin boat on Tuesday and asked, in bad German, for the address of a bookshop in Berlin. The bookshop belongs to the party. In the suitcase, under two shirts and a Bible, are [+ lw_name +]: enough, the treasurer reckons, to keep the party's papers and organisers going for months.

There is no letter, only a slip of paper with a number on it and the initials of the Executive's treasurer. Money from Moscow never comes with conditions, and never comes without them.

- @all: Take it all for the apparatus.
- @strikes: Take it for the strike funds and the papers only.
- @return: Send most of it back.

@all
subtitle: [+ lw_amount +] funds. Moscow will know exactly what we owe it, and if the courier talks, so will the police.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources += Q.lw_amount;
Q.independence -= 6;
RG.ecci('all', 2);
if (Math.random() < 0.2) {
    Q.lw_out = 1;
    Q.spd_relation -= 5;
    Q.worker_support -= 2;
    Q.repression += 4;
    RG.news('Police seize Bolshevik diamonds: communists in the pay of Moscow', 3);
    RG.ledger('The police caught a Comintern courier with Moscow\'s money for the party.', 'lw_gold');
}
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 1, 2);
!}

The treasurer locks it in a safe in a flat in Charlottenburg, and the party pays its printers on time for the first time this year. [? if lw_out = 1 : A week later the sailor is arrested drunk in Hamburg, and talks. The nationalist papers have a field day with "Moscow gold". ?]

@strikes
subtitle: 1 fund now, and solidarity money for the districts. A smaller debt.
on-arrival: {!
Q.resources += 1;
Q.independence -= 2;
for (var d of Q.districts) {
    if (Q['district_' + d + '_strike']) { RG.district(d, {loyalty: 4}); }
}
Q.worker_support += 1;
RG.ecci('all', 1);
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 2);
!}

The Zentrale takes what it needs for the papers and puts the rest into a solidarity fund for strikers, with accounts that any district can inspect. Moscow asks for receipts. It gets them.

@return
subtitle: Our independence grows. The Spartacists are proud; the Executive is puzzled and offended.
on-arrival: {!
Q.independence += 8;
RG.ecci('all', -4);
RG.lw.lean('luxemburgist', 1, 5);
RG.lw.lean('offensive', 0, -3);
!}

The sailor goes back to Stettin with his suitcase a good deal lighter than it came, and a letter from the Zentrale: the German party thanks the Executive and will live on its members' dues.
